==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mythical Titan Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Jamiera Cat''' at level 20+10 using [[Normal Cat Capsule|Cat Tickets]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Titan Cat has high health and attack power, as well as moderate attack speed. Use him to tank for long-ranged cats like [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]], [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|UFO Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], or to break past groups of enemies. His area attacks and good stats allow him to be a formidable force against long ranged enemies and, in general, in stages that do not rely on high DPS on the frontline.

His range is quite short, so try clearing fodder enemies when summoning him to give him more time to hit the bosses without getting killed too early. Although the short range sometimes prevents him from staying on the battlefield, it allows this Cat to shine against enemies with Long Distance attacks, as he can easily damage enemies within their blindspots without worry.

As a Normal Cat, Titan Cat also has a decent amount of [[Cat Combo]]s to his disposal as well.

==='''True Form'''===
In True Form, Jamiera Cat's stats skyrocket, doubling what it was originally. This increases Jamiera's use spectacularly across the board, at the cost of a slightly longer recharging time. Luckily, that does not matter, as explained below.

First off, in late [[Stories of Legend]] and even some of the easier [[Uncanny Legends]] stages, Jamiera Cat is most useful as a defense/meatshield type cat than for his power. While his damage might pale in comparison to other reliable attackers, his singular knockback allows him to hold the line for quite a while. Unfortunately, unlike early-game, his role as an attacker is done better by other non-uber and gacha units, such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] or [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]]; he also faces competition as a generalist tanker from [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] and [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]], not to mention other alternatives.

Despite this, Jamiera Cat's insanely high stats and [[Knockback]] ability make him crucial during earlier parts of the game, such as [[Flappy Cat (Insane)|Flappy Cat]], [[Mammals? (Insane)|Mammals?]] and [[Crazy Cats (Insane)|Crazy Cats]]. Furthermore, his high health and damage as well as only having one knockback mean that Jamiera is good against backliners like [[Master A.]], [[Camelle]], [[Sunfish Jones]] or [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]], as he can walk into their range and land several hits. However, his low speed is a problem against [[Professor A.]] or [[Henry]], whose [[Slow|slow]] and [[Freeze|freeze]] ability (respectively), will cripple him if they occur.

