==Trivia==
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.4 Update|Version 2.0.4]] reduced Jamiera Cat's base health from 3,000 to 2,000 and base attack from 840 to 560, and increased base recharge from 810f<sup>27s</sup> to 930f<sup>31s</sup>.
*Jamiera Cat gained the [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] target in [[Version 2.9.1 Update|Version 2.9.1]]. Typically this happens in the same update as the trait is introduced, but Angel was added in [[Version 2.7 Update|Version 2.7]].
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Jamiera Cat was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Five Hearts (Removed Combo)|Five Hearts]].
*In the English Version, the text on Jamiera Cat's t-shirt reads "I love Mackerel" in Japanese.
*Since he's included in [[Jibbly Studio (Combo)|Jibbly Studio]], Mythical Titan Cat could be a reference to the newborn [[wikia:nausicaa:God Warriors|god warrior]] from the Studio Ghibli film ''[[wikipedia:Nausicaä of the Valley of the Wind|Nausicaä of the Valley of the Wind]]''.
*He had a child with [[Kerihime (Special Cat)|Kerihime]], making [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Baby Cat]].
**Additionally, because of the [[Treasured Grandchild (Combo)|Treasured Grandchild]] Cat Combo, [[Kung Fu Cat X (Rare Cat)|Kung Fu Cat X]] is likely Titan Cat's father.
*[[Squish Ball Cat (Special Cat)|Muscleman Cat]] is also a distant relative of Titan Cat, according to its description.
*Mythical Titan Cat's Japanese name, Neko Darabotchi, is a reference to [[wikipedia:Daidarabotchi|Daidarabotchi]], one of the biggest creatures in ''yōkai'' folklore.
*Jamiera Cat may be a reference to the ''Ultraman'' monster [[wikia:ultra:Jamila|Jamila]]. This is further supported by the Japanese names of the two characters, where two syllables from the monster's name are swapped to form the Cat's name:
**'''<u>ジャミラ</u>''' ''Jamira'' →　ネコ'''<u>ジャラミ</u> '''Neko ''Jarami''.
***Also, in Japanese popular culture, the monster is often represented by placing one's shirt over their head like Jamiera Cat does.
*In [[The Battle Cats POP!]], and in much older versions of [[The Battle Cats]], Jamiera Cat faced left instead of right in his icon.
*In The Battle Cats POP!, Jamiera Cat's name is mispelled as Jameira Cat.
*In [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)]], Titan Cat is named "Giant Warrior-Cat". His Evolved Form is named "Mythical Giant-Cat".
*Prior to [[Version 15.5 Update|Version 15.5]], Titan Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Titan Cat
Blessed with extreme attack power and
ridiculous amounts of health (Area Attack) </pre>
<pre>Mythical Titan Cat
Lord of Destruction (?) (Area Attack)
Extreme attack power and health. </pre>
<pre>Jamiera Cat
Might knockback enemies. (Area Attack)
The Real Lord of Destruction?
Don't stretch your shirt like this. </pre>

